  "solution": "To find the remainder when  \n\\[\nP(x)=6x^3-15x^2+21x-23\n\\]\nis divided by \\(3x-6\\), use the Remainder Theorem.\n\nSet the divisor equal to zero:\n\\[\n3x-6=0 \\implies x=2\n\\]\n\nThe remainder is \\(P(2)\\):\n\\[\nP(2)=6(2)^3-15(2)^2+21(2)-23\n\\]\n\\[\n=6(8)-15(4)+42-23\n\\]\n\\[\n=48-60+42-23\n\\]\n\\[\n=7\n\\]\n\nSo the remainder is \\(7\\).\n\nThe answer is 7.",
